# invasion-1796-french: 1796 as the French, one player, Tactical off. The fleet at Bordeaux sails
# to Amsterdam, a neutral port of a minor nation. In the next turn the Ships menu offers Invasion
# (navy, WON2.BM: two or more ships at a neutral port whose owner is above 6), and the invasion
# places a new army there. The player then only ends turns until the game ends, as the generated
# games do. No session reaches an invasion (tests/README.md). Written by hand.
#! seed 1

# A TICK: any key ends it. A pause that waits for a key: a space. The End Turn question and
# the End Game question: Yes. A retreat the player is asked to choose: Esc.
rule 3 key f12
rule 1 key space
rule 2:E text y
rule 2:R key esc

# The built-in title, then the start menu: Start NEW Game, 1796.
play until 2:W
text s
prompt
key enter

# Utility: swap to the French, Tactical off.
play until 2:M
digest
text u
prompt
text a
prompt
text t
prompt
key esc

# Ships, Sail, Amsterdam (the first port of the list), then End Turn.
play until 2:M
text s
prompt
text s
prompt
# shot sail-to
state
key enter
play until 2:M
digest
text e

# The next turn: Ships offers Invasion; it places a new army in Amsterdam.
play until 2:M
digest
text s
prompt
# shot ships-invasion
state
text i
prompt
# shot invaded
state
key space

# Each of the 9 turns left: a digest at the main menu, then End Turn.
repeat 9
play until 2:M
digest
text e
end

# The game ends: the Battle Summary, the Hall of Fame and Game Over. The start menu: Quit to
# DOS, and a key for END's "Press any key to continue".
play until 2:W
digest
text q
repeat space
